---
import PageHeader from '../components/PageHeader.astro';
import { adobeFontsKitId, links, site } from '../config/site';
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout title="Privacy" description="How Emet Labs handles data on this website and in trace-grab.">
	<PageHeader title="Privacy">
		<p class="text-small text-dusk">Last updated 10 November 2026</p>
	</PageHeader>

	<section class="border-t border-line">
		<div class="wrap grid py-16 sm:py-20 lg:grid-cols-12">
			<div class="prose-emet measure lg:col-span-9 lg:col-start-4">
				<h2>This website</h2>
				<p>
					We do not use advertising cookies, tracking pixels or third-party analytics on this website,
					and we do not sell or share visitor data. The site is hosted on GitHub Pages, which processes
					standard request information, such as IP addresses, to serve it.
				</p>
				{
					adobeFontsKitId && (
						<p>
							Some typefaces on this site are served by Adobe Fonts. When your browser requests them,
							Adobe receives standard request information, such as your IP address, and counts page
							views for font licensing. That processing is governed by Adobe’s privacy policy.
						</p>
					)
				}

				<h2>trace-grab</h2>
				<p>
					<strong>trace-grab</strong> runs on your machine; its only network access is an optional LangSmith API source that you enable yourself. It has no upload command,
					contains no Emet Labs endpoint, and has no telemetry, analytics or update check. If you choose
					to share a corpus with us, that transfer happens by a method you control. See{' '}
					<a href={links.traceGrabTransfer} target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Sending your corpus<span class="sr-only"> (opens in a new tab)</span></a>{' '}
					for what happens after a corpus is received.
				</p>
				<p>
					Tokenized output is pseudonymized, not anonymized: someone holding the key that stays on your
					machine, or the original data, can re-identify it.
				</p>

				<h2>Sentinel</h2>
				<p>
					<strong>Sentinel</strong> is in private development. Before it is generally available, this
					page will describe what data it processes, where that data is stored and how long it is kept.
				</p>

				<h2>Questions</h2>
				<p>For privacy questions, contact <a href={links.email}>{site.email}</a>.</p>
			</div>
		</div>
	</section>
</BaseLayout>
